.TH AWS-KILLSWITCH 1 "2026-09" "aws-killswitch" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aws-killswitch \- stop an AWS account spending, without losing anything
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aws-killswitch
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aws-killswitch
stops the parts of an AWS account that cost money \(em compute, not storage \(em
and records enough state to put every one of them back. Stateful storage (S3,
EFS, DynamoDB, EBS volumes, snapshots and backups) is never touched under any
flag.
.PP
Nothing changes without
.BR \-\-yes .
Without it every command is a dry run that reports what it would have done.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B plan
Report what would be stopped, and what would deliberately not be.
.TP
.B fire
Stop it. Requires
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.B status
What is currently stopped, and any deadlines attached to it.
.TP
.BI restore " plan"
Put everything back, from the named plan id (see
.BR "aws-killswitch status" ).
.TP
.B spend
Month-to-date cost against the configured threshold.
.TP
.B verify
Fire, read the account back, restore, read it back again, and report every
divergence.
.B "SCRATCH ACCOUNTS ONLY"
\(em this fires for real.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " PATH"
Policy file (default
.IR ./killswitch.json ).
.TP
.BI \-state " URI"
Where snapshots live:
.IR s3://bucket/prefix .
Overrides the config.
.TP
.BI \-local " DIR"
Local snapshot copy (default
.IR ~/.aws-killswitch ).
.TP
.BI \-audit " PATH"
Append-only log (default
.IR ~/.aws-killswitch/audit.jsonl ).
.TP
.BI \-threshold " USD"
For
.BR spend :
exit non-zero above this figure.
.TP
.B \-yes
Actually make changes. Without it everything is a dry run.
.TP
.B \-force
Proceed past the blast-radius threshold and any warnings.
.TP
.B \-json
Machine-readable output.
.TP
.BI \-settle " DURATION"
For
.BR verify :
how long to let the account settle before reading it back (default 90s).
.TP
.B \-plan\-only
For
.BR verify :
plan and report coverage, change nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error: wrong invocation, or a refusal to run as asked.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./killswitch.json
Default policy file.
.TP
.I ~/.aws-killswitch/audit.jsonl
Append-only record of every run.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
See what firing would stop, changing nothing:
.PP
.RS
.B aws-killswitch plan
.RE
.PP
Stop the account, for real:
.PP
.RS
.B aws-killswitch fire \-\-yes
.RE
.PP
Put it back:
.PP
.RS
.B aws-killswitch restore \fIPLAN-ID\fB
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/aws-killswitch
.UE
